# Per-package statement-coverage floor, in percent.
#
# F-23 (docs/security-hardening.md §3): three of the packages that handle
# untrusted input shipped at 0.0 % coverage. This file is the ratchet -- CI
# fails when a package drops below its recorded floor, so coverage can only go
# up. The values are the measured baseline of the v1.1.1 audit, rounded down.
#
# auth/oidc, auth/webauthn and provider sit at 0 deliberately: the §6 test
# programme raises them in a later phase, and the gate is written to read this
# file so raising a floor is a one-line change here, not a code change.
#
# Format: <package path relative to the module root> <floor percent>
audit 50
auth/basic 80
auth/jwt 85
auth/oidc 0
auth/totp 78
auth/webauthn 0
middleware 30
provider 0
session 80
storage 75
